{
  "_meta": {
    "updated": "2026-08-10",
    "note": "Species classification behind the Pokemon GO in-game search keywords 'legendary', 'mythical' and 'ultra beast'/'ultra beasts', plus the region-locked ('regional') roster. Keyed by the species ids used in ../../pogoaccs/data/species.json; every entry carries its Pokedex number. legendary/mythical/ultraBeast are transcribed from Niantic's own pokemonClass field in the GAME_MASTER (POKEMON_CLASS_LEGENDARY / _MYTHIC / _ULTRA_BEAST) - the field the in-game search keyword reads - restricted to forms released in Pokemon GO. 'regional' is NOT a game search keyword; it is the region-locked roster, curated from pokemongo.fandom + Serebii. Categories overlap on purpose: Uxie/Mesprit/Azelf are legendary AND regional, and seven Ultra Beasts are also regional. Mega and Primal forms are listed under their base species' category (pokemongo.fandom lists Mega Latias, Primal Kyogre, Mega Diancie etc. in those same tables). Entries with partial:true are region-locked in only SOME of their released forms - read the entry note before treating them as regional. Entries with released:false are correctly-classified forms that sources say are not obtainable yet. See SOURCES.md for the full cross-check log.",
    "sources": [
      "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeMiners/game_masters/master/latest/latest.json",
      "https://pogoapi.net/api/v1/pokemon_rarity.json",
      "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pvpoke/pvpoke/master/src/data/gamemaster.json",
      "https://pokemongo.fandom.com/wiki/Legendary_Pok%C3%A9mon",
      "https://pokemongo.fandom.com/wiki/Mythical_Pok%C3%A9mon",
      "https://pokemongo.fandom.com/wiki/Ultra_Beast",
      "https://pokemongo.fandom.com/wiki/Region-exclusive_Pok%C3%A9mon",
      "https://serebii.net/pokemongo/exclusives.shtml"
    ],
